b=Book('02','Architecture & Engineering','Architecture-Engineering','Runtime boundaries, frontend and backend design, integration contracts, and the API map.');b.intro()
b.section('System topology and source ownership','''The confirmed hosting platform is Railway. The main deployable is a Next.js App Router application with browser components, route handlers and server-domain modules. Supabase supplies identity and PostgreSQL persistence; private Cloudflare R2 is the production media path. External providers supply AI, web research, social delivery, website integrations and payment processing.

The repository also contains Python intelligence packages and a separate FastAPI/Celery Social Distribution Engine. Their presence does not prove they run in the current Railway environment. The active TypeScript GEO scanner can run through the web runtime and database-driven hooks. Build the separate services only for selected execution paths. Older Amplify, Oracle tunnel, Lightsail or research deployment notes are not the owner's confirmed current hosting topology.''',('Dockerfile','next.config.ts','src/app','src/server','backend','Social-Distribtion-Engine-MelloxAI-SDE','docs/repository-layout.md'))
b.diagram('Browser: React pages + editorial UI','Next.js routes / RPC / protected callbacks','Auth + workspace role + validation + rate limit','Domain services + billing + durable job records','Supabase / private R2 / external providers','Webhooks + cron workers reconcile final state')
b.table(['Layer','Owns','Must not own'],[['src/app + components','Navigation, forms, loading and review UI','Service credentials or authoritative delivery state'],['src/lib','Shared contracts, pure rules, helpers; explicitly named server modules also exist here','Assume every lib file is browser-safe'],['src/server + route handlers','Trust checks, external operations, job execution, metering','Trust client role/workspace/price assertions'],['Supabase','Identity, state, RLS, atomic claims, ledger durability','Infer business completion from a browser view'],['R2','Private generated and uploaded media','Public uncontrolled access to all client assets'],['Python / SDR','Separate optional runtime boundaries','Assume main Next gateway rules apply automatically']],[1,2,2])
b.section('Frontend composition and navigation','''Route entry points live in src/app. Product surfaces live mainly in src/components/app, with shared UI, workspace and brand components. Workspace paths are generated through src/lib/workspace rather than assembled ad hoc. Public pages can avoid loading the full authenticated provider tree; providers.tsx distinguishes public paths and dynamically loads AppProviders.

TanStack Query handles server data and cache invalidation. Query keys include workspace identity, and workspace switching clears the affected cache. Local component state owns transient editing, not canonical publication status. Mutation completion invalidates the matching scoped reads. Async work retains the ID captured when the request started.

The UI stack is React 19, Tailwind 4, Radix primitives, Framer Motion, Lucide, Recharts and Sonner. Existing EmptyState, ErrorState, Skeleton and AppModalShell patterns should be reused. Every async feature needs loading, empty, failed, unavailable/disabled and successful states. A pending edit must not be lost when an older fetch resolves.

Next.js behavior must be read from the installed node_modules/next/dist/docs version. The current config enables standalone output and names external server packages for parsing and rendering. New features should preserve the server/client import boundary and current routing conventions rather than importing a server module into a client component.''',('src/app/providers.tsx','src/app/AppProviders.tsx','src/lib/workspace','src/components/app','next.config.ts','node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/01-getting-started/05-server-and-client-components.md'))
b.section('Authenticated route kernel and RPC','''defineRoute centralizes authenticated HTTP handling. Its order is authentication, schema parsing, workspace membership/minimum role, rate limiting and handler. User-authenticated routes can attribute a workspace header only after membership checks; workspace routes resolve an explicit ID from validated input. The handler receives the caller's RLS-bound Supabase client, request context and abort signal.

The RPC route /api/rpc/[...fn] dispatches through src/server/fns/index.ts. Client stubs call registered server functions rather than importing server implementation. A server function combines authentication middleware, Zod input validation, role checks and a domain service. The route name, not a client-selected implementation name, decides what executes.

The main kernel maps BillingError to HTTP 402, budget exhaustion to 429, malformed input or blocked URLs to 400, oversized bodies to 413, auth failures to 401, role denials to the owning 403 path, and stale editorial conflicts to 409. Provider errors are normalized; internal stack traces, balances, keys and raw provider messages are not the response contract. Streaming endpoints also need correct cancellation and settlement behavior.''',('src/server/route.ts','src/server/server-fn.ts','src/server/fns/index.ts','src/app/api/rpc','src/server/request-context.ts'))
b.h('Recommended contract for a new workspace mutation')
b.bullets('Accept a workspace UUID and only feature-owned input fields; validate lengths, formats and allowed enum values.','Authenticate and require the operation-specific role before any paid provider call or privileged read.','Load each referenced row inside that workspace, even when the supplied item ID is a valid UUID.','Check feature availability, quota, balance, safety and idempotency before producing a side effect.','Write using the read revision or an atomic state transition, and return a stable domain result.','Map failure without leaking raw upstream bodies; preserve retryable and ambiguous outcomes in durable state.')
b.section('Persistence, ownership and transactions','''Supabase PostgreSQL is the durable source of truth for workspace, brand, content, approval, job, usage, account and connector state. Generated TypeScript Row/Insert/Update types help clients use that schema; they are not a replacement for migrations, SQL constraints, grants or RLS.

Most customer records carry workspace_id, and their policies check membership or role helpers. The user client carries the caller's JWT and uses RLS. Service-role clients bypass RLS, so every privileged service path must validate the workspace and row relationship explicitly. Ownership columns are protected in important domains to stop records being moved across tenants.

Concurrent workflows use atomic claims, database functions, leases and revision checks. Lease duration is not proof the worker is alive; another worker may reclaim expired work. Idempotency must surround the external operation and its stored provider ID, not just the first HTTP request. Financial holds, capture, release and grants require transaction-safe functions and stable replay keys.

Volume 06 contains the full checked-in table/column dictionary, foreign-key relationships, database function names and migration chronology. It intentionally avoids pretending generated types encode every runtime policy. Start a clean database from the canonical migration sequence and verify it, rather than create approximate tables by hand from this PDF.''',('supabase/migrations','src/integrations/supabase/types.ts','src/integrations/supabase/client.user.server.ts','src/integrations/supabase/client.server.ts'))
b.section('Long-running jobs and reconciliation','''Generation, scans, analytics synchronization, competitor research, audience runs, Autopilot steps and media completion outlive an ordinary click. The request stores a job and may start a bounded after() continuation. Cron hooks reclaim or advance work that timed out or survived a process restart.

The run-schedules hook is a shared coordinator: scheduled jobs and due Market Brain collections each have bounded batch reads, while Autopilot and Audience have bounded execution budgets. It also schedules refresh of social trends, audience outcome collection, visual capture and expired-memory cleanup. Dedicated hooks advance GEO, UGC, distribution reconciliation, experiments, billing and operational checks.

Separate concerns: generation produces a reviewed artifact, publishing sends approved content, and reconciliation determines delivery truth. A timeout after submitting to a provider is an ambiguous side effect. Record and investigate the task rather than charging or posting again blindly. Terminal states must win over stale callbacks, and retries must not invalidate a newer user's edit.''',('src/app/api/public/hooks/run-schedules/route.ts','src/server/cron.ts','src/server/studio/runner.server.ts','src/server/ugc/providers/routed.server.ts','src/lib/postforme'))
b.section('Media data flow and storage contracts','''The canonical storage adapter writes new production assets to R2 when configured. Keys include workspace/<workspaceId>/assets/r2/<assetId>/...; older keys without the r2 marker can remain in Supabase Storage. Reader and deletion logic chooses the correct backend from canonical identity, with server-only aliases for migrations.

Media persistence validates supported formats, size, ownership and idempotency. A persistence lease prevents concurrent overwrites; an expired process's lease can be reclaimed atomically. Replaying an old persistence request must not restore an intentionally deleted asset. User uploads and report logos also use the canonical storage layer.

The browser asks authenticated routes for short-lived access. The download route obtains a fresh five-minute attachment URL after membership and workspace-path checks, letting the browser navigate directly without buffering a large video. Private buckets stay private. Canvas or fetch use of signed URLs still requires approved GET/HEAD CORS origins. A signed URL is a temporary access artifact, never the permanent database identity of media.''',('src/server/assets/storage.server.ts','src/server/assets','src/app/api/assets/download/route.ts','docs/storage.md','docs/storage-migration.md'))
