b.section('OAuth, callbacks and connector state','''Connector installation starts in an authenticated workspace context and binds provider authorization to the initiating user and workspace. One-use state, expiration, safe internal return paths and membership rechecks protect callbacks. Provider tokens stay in encrypted server-only credential storage; browser responses contain status and validated destinations rather than raw credentials.

Canva uses PKCE and serialized installation/refresh/withdrawal. Notion adds callback browser binding and an atomic operation lease around imports/exports. Keep the service-role-derived encryption root stable across deploys, or preserve a configured legacy dedicated key until grants are replaced. Rotating a key without a migration can make existing grants unreadable.

Readiness is capability-specific. A valid OAuth grant does not prove sufficient scopes, selected data source, provider app verification or usable write permissions. Disconnection removes local grants and attempts provider invalidation where supported; a provider without revocation may require user action in that provider. Imported content has its own retained lifecycle.''',('src/server/connectors/canva','src/server/connectors/notion','src/server/analytics/google','docs/canva-integration.md','docs/notion-integration.md'))
b.section('AI Visibility engineering','''The main app's pure GEO engine separates fetching from deterministic evaluation. analyze-page builds structured evidence; rules consume page/site context; score calculates points; fix recipes and proposal services translate findings into actions. Stable rule IDs and fingerprints preserve finding state across scans.

Current scoring gives pass 1, warning 0.5, failure 0, and excludes not-applicable rules. Category scores are weighted means of applicable rule credit, then the six category shares create the overall score. Shares are AI access 20%, technical 20%, structured data 15%, content 20%, authority 20% and rendering/performance 5%. SCORE_VERSION is 2; different versions must not be presented as ordinary score movement.

Priority combines impact, confidence and effort: 0.5 x impact + 0.25 x confidence + 0.25 x (1 - effortValue). Effort values are low .25, medium .5 and high .75. Thresholds are .8 critical, .6 high, .4 medium. Rule confidence and an emerging convention do not become proof of causal search ranking influence.

Full scans persist a frontier and checkpoint under leases; browser rendering is a separately controlled fallback for empty client shells. All page requests and redirects go through safe fetching. A fix applies only within the connected source's verified ownership boundary and requires post-change verification.''',('src/lib/geo/analyze-page.ts','src/lib/geo/rules.ts','src/lib/geo/score.ts','src/lib/geo/types.ts','src/server/geo','src/server/safe-fetch.ts'))
b.section('Separate Python intelligence and SDR runtimes','''The backend package is a Python/FastAPI analysis and persistence runtime with crawler, connector, content/entity/fix/opportunity/validation packages. It has its own adapter and configuration surface. Its provider adapters must not be described as active main-app model routes. Some Python model defaults and historical documents reference older generations; their production use and provider availability were not confirmed, so they are excluded from the current main-app model recommendation.

The Social Distribution Engine has its own Docker/Compose and Railway API, worker and beat configuration files. It is an independently tested service with provider OAuth, delivery and multi-tenant concerns. The main app's default Post for Me path does not require deploying this service solely because its files are present.

For a rebuild, retain a separate service only if the selected feature path needs it. Otherwise duplicate queues, provider credentials and databases create extra operational state without improving the editorial product. Any consolidation requires a migration plan for existing records and callbacks; file location alone is not permission to remove a runtime.''',('backend','crawler','connectors','Social-Distribtion-Engine-MelloxAI-SDE/README.md','Social-Distribtion-Engine-MelloxAI-SDE/railway.toml'))
